    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d815-a1">

                <pb facs="0758" n="746" sameAs="frus:frus1944v05/pg746"/>

                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Enclosure—Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The King of Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Ibn Saud</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the American Minister</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Eddy</hi>)<anchor n="67" xml:id="d815-f1"/>
                </head>
                <p>We have received with pleasure Your Excellencies’ joint letter, dated September
                    18, 1944,<anchor n="68" xml:id="d815-f2"/> by which you transmitted to us the
                    decision of the two friendly governments, Great Britain and the United States of
                    America, concerning their help to us in supply matters for our country, and
                    their joint agreement to increase the quantity of cereals, which has been
                    decided as a supply to this country, from 40,000 tons to 50,000 tons. We are
                    sincerely thankful for the two friendly governments for their endeavor in
                    assisting us and appreciate their nice attention and fine help for our country.
                    We have already ordered our Minister of Finance, Abdullah Suleiman, to state the
                    remarks we have regarding this matter.</p>
                <p>Accept our highest regards.</p>
                <closer><dateline rendition="#float-left">Written on <date
                            calendar="hijri gregorian" when="1944-10-02">Shawal 14, 1363 (October 2,
                            1944)</date>.</dateline></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d815-f1" n="67" type="source" xml:id="d815-f1-content">
                <p>Sent also to the British Chargé in Saudi Arabia (Ellison).</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d815-f2" n="68" xml:id="d815-f2-content">
                <p>See telegram 177, September 12, 5 p.m., to Jidda, <ref target="#pg739">p.
                        739</ref>.</p>
            </note>
